WEBVTT

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.120
Hangar, Galar Region

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.360
Rose, Macro Cosmos Chairman

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.530
Olive, Rose's Secretary

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:19.830
What’s wrong?
Olive, Rose's Secretary

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:19.840
What’s wrong?

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:24.810
When we had the core absorb
Galar particles, it started overloading.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.980
That’s why we have the hangar, no?

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.470
Well... The energy tore through
the hangar.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.850
You intend to release it again?

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:58.440
Hurry and reinforce the hangar.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:00:59.150
Ma’am!

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:04.750
Truly unlimited energy...

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.900
Marvelous...

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.390
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:15.490
I win!

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:16.660
Off you go, then.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:17.360
Darn.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.230
I’m turning off the light, then.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:21.730
Okay.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.320
Thanks, Pikachu.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.040
Hmm...

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:56.610
Trainers in the Galar Region use these bands
to Daimax, or gigantify Pokémon.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:02:00.840
But there are still many things
unknown about the exact mechanism.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.190
I’ve been wondering about it
for ages, too.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:07.040
Why do Pokémon Daimax
to begin with?

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.340
Yeah, now that you mention it...

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:15.750
And Daimaxing is limited to
the Wild Area and Stadiums, right?

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.590
I don’t really understand
that either.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:19.690
Right...

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:22.670
There have been
a number of exceptions, actually.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:23.910
Exceptions?

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.200
Pokémon Daimaxing
outside of the Wild Area and Stadiums.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.700
There have been many
reported cases as of late.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:36.710
I wonder if it has something to do
with my Daimax Band shining...

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.800
Anything we’re curious about,
we go straight to check out!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:42.500
That’s our job as
research fellows, yeah?

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.110
He’s correct.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:45.950
Go, Satoshi...

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:49.720
Head to the Galar Region,
to solve the mystery of Daimax.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.000
Got it!

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:43.230
Satoshi and Go have come to Galar, and are headed
for Brassie Town to solve the mystery of Daimax.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.950
Train journeys have a special
charm to them, don’t they?

00:04:46.950 --> 00:04:48.170
For sure.

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:50.340
Since we’re in Galar,
I just had to get these!

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.240
The nice-smelling tiny thingies!

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.300
We’ve gotta kick things off
with some of these!

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.360
Here, Pikachu, have one.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.410
Scones?

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:00.020
Time to eat!

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:05.040
Here, some milk tea.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.750
Fhanks.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:09.760
Honestly, did you forget
why we’re here?

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:13.370
I remember!

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:17.570
We’re going to meet a friend of
Director Sakuragi’s in Brassie Town, right?

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.040
Her name was...

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.320
Professor Magnolia.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.810
The number one Daimax researcher.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:25.110
Oh, yeah, right!

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.000
We apologize for the inconvenience.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:34.310
The train will stop here for some time,
due to a thick fog up ahead.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.950
Fog?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.960
Don’t really see
anything from here...

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:51.830
We’re expecting to be here for a long time,
so we will open some of the doors.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:06:00.160
What a mess. We get held up here
when we’re so close...

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:12.210
Horubee! Digging Pokémon!
Normal type!

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.540
It’s very sensitive to danger,

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:19.330
and the sound of Armorgaw’s flapping will have it
digging a hole to hide underground in moments!

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.270
My chance at catching it!

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.340
C’mon, Go!

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:33.930
It’s going in the forest!

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:38.160
It’s called the Slumbering Weald...

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.720
What an amazing name...

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:41.130
Hold it!

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:45.440
The Slumbering Weald

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.080
Where did the Horubee go?
The Slumbering Weald

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.160
Where did the Horubee go?

00:06:49.490 --> 00:06:51.570
This fog’s thicker than I thought.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:53.090
Horubee!

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.910
There!

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.780
Horubee!

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:10.380
Monster Ball, Go!

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.100
Horubee’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:28.830
I caught it, Satoshi!

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.050
Huh?

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:32.760
Satoshi?

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.650
Go?

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:40.610
Where are you?

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:43.620
What is it, Pikachu?

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:23.050
A Pokémon I’ve never seen before...

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:29.070
No matching Pokémon
found in past data.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:31.240
So it’s a new species of Pokémon?!

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:07.230
What’s that...?

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:12.740
No registered data for this Pokémon!
Unable to analyze!

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:16.450
That means...
It’s a new species of Pokémon?!

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:25.400
Just what I hoped for!

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.550
Let’s battle!

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:32.800
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:42.870
I’ll catch you! Go!

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:46.360
W-What?!

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:53.360
Rabbifoot, use Ember!

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:00.950
It went right through...

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.820
What’s going on?

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:16.780
Not good...

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:25.420
Messon, Rabbifoot,
stay close to me.

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:44.970
Where am I?

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:48.370
Right, Satoshi!

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.480
Satoshi!

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:51.960
Where are you?

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:55.950
Satoshi!

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:03.080
Satoshi!

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:08.150
Maybe he went back to
the train without me...

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:11.190
Rotom, call Satoshi.

00:11:11.190 --> 00:11:12.570
Okay!

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:22.380
Calling!

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.330
Guess I shouldn’t have expected him
to answer the phone...

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.770
Calling!
Guess I shouldn’t have expected him
to answer the phone...

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:28.240
Oh no!

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:50.140
What’re those...?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.660
They look like the light
you see during Daimax.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:01.860
Oh dear, even out here?

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:22.330
Why was I sleeping here?

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:24.370
Where’s that Pokémon?!

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:28.470
I better get back
to the train soon...

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:36.480
Go! Are you here, Go?!

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:42.430
I won’t make it back aboard
in time like this...

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:47.040
Go could’ve gone on ahead,
I’ll have to take the chance.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.740
Maru-chan,
here’s some Oran Berries.

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.760
Maruyakude?

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.240
What’s going on?

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:22.260
Kyodaimaxing
in the middle of town?!

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.140
I don’t know either!

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:35.110
No, Maruyakude!

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:37.150
Stop, Maru-chan!

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.220
Chairman Rose.

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:58.890
The second burst of energy
that tore through the hangar...

00:13:58.890 --> 00:14:02.530
...is causing Pokémon around Galar
to grow giant and start rampaging.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:07.690
A few casualties are inevitable.

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:11.980
This is all for Galar’s future.

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:22.140
Sorry, coming through!

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:27.150
This isn’t the Wild Area
or a Stadium, so why...?

00:14:27.150 --> 00:14:30.980
It glowed red and
Kyodaimaxed all on its own.

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:35.280
Then it stopped
listening to me, its trainer...

00:14:36.660 --> 00:14:39.090
What happened to you,
Maru-chan?

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:41.600
You were so friendly before...

00:14:42.370 --> 00:14:48.430
Maruyakude. Kyodaimax form.
Radiator Pokemon. Fire/Bug-type.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:51.210
Its body temperature
reaches over 1,000 degrees Celsius.

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:53.410
Its heat waves incinerate its enemies.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:55.650
We’ll sort it out!

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:56.910
Everyone, wait here!

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:59.730
Stop! Don’t be so reckless!

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:00.970
I’ll be fine!

00:15:00.970 --> 00:15:01.950
Kid!

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:09.950
Maruyakude! Stop it!

00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:12.680
Everyone’s scared!

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:14.680
So please, stop rampaging!

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:33.930
Maruyakude, you must have
a reason for doing this, right?

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:40.880
I have to...
I have to do something...

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:43.080
Pikachu! Let’s do it!

00:15:43.850 --> 00:15:45.170
Riolu, you too!

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.920
Pikachu, use Electroweb!
Riolu, use Vacuum Wave!

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:15.570
No way...

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:24.320
Kairyu! I choose you!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.760
Kairyu! Hurricane!

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:35.790
Pikachu, use Electroweb!

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:37.630
Riolu, use Vacuum Wave!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:06.170
Ugh...

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:08.660
It didn’t do anything...

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:18.540
This... This is kinda bad.

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.430
Everyone, run for it!

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.970
Lizardon! Rock Seal!

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:38.120
Mr. Dande!

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:41.310
Satoshi!
Leave the rest to me!

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:43.810
Okay!

00:17:43.810 --> 00:17:45.720
Kairyu, you hear that?

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:53.070
Lizardon! Air Slash!

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:08.120
Mr. Dande is so awesome...

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.850
Maru-chan!

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:26.080
I’m glad you’re okay,
Maru-chan...

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:31.910
Thank you. You saved us.

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:34.040
Maruyakude,
we were worried about you.

00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:36.300
Mr. Dande!

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:40.680
The odd gleam in its eyes
has left, too.

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:42.710
I’d expect nothing less
from Mr. Dande!

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:44.070
You really are the hero of Galar!

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:46.050
Thank you! Thank you!

00:18:46.050 --> 00:18:49.560
I only did what any Champion
would have done.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:55.500
As for the string of rampaging
Daimax Pokémon lately...

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:57.570
I hope to find the cause
as soon as possible,

00:18:57.570 --> 00:18:59.860
and make sure
it doesn’t happen again.

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:03.590
So until then, everyone,
please prioritize your own safety.

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:04.670
<i>Yes!</i>

00:19:05.250 --> 00:19:06.190
Lizardon!

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:12.080
Mr. Dande, where are you going?

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:16.450
To stop the Daimax Pokémon
that are rampaging elsewhere.

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:19.020
Let us help you too!

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:22.270
I appreciate the sentiment, but...

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:23.590
Please!

00:19:29.490 --> 00:19:30.850
Understood.

00:19:31.320 --> 00:19:33.340
Let’s get going, then!

00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:34.160
Sure!

00:19:55.810 --> 00:19:58.670
Ms. Sonia, your driving isn’t exactly...

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:02.130
How rude.
It’s just this beaten-up car.

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:06.930
Oh, right. Rotom, call Satoshi.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.310
Okay!

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:15.900
Incoming call from Go.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.910
Hello? Go? Where are you?

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:21.650
You picked up! Same to you,
Satoshi, where are you?!

00:20:22.520 --> 00:20:26.860
I’m headed to stop the rampaging
Daimax Pokémon with Mr. Dande.

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:28.160
You’re with Mr. Dande?!

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:30.320
Yeah. So much happened.

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:32.160
A lot happened to me too.

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:35.770
I’m on my way to the ruins
in Turf Town with Ms. Sonia.

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:36.920
Ms. Sonia?

00:20:36.920 --> 00:20:39.420
You know, from Shoot Stadium!

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:42.000
The woman we met
by the statue of the hero!

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:45.380
Right! Wasn’t she investigating
a legend or something?

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:49.770
Yeah. The Daimax Pokémon
rampaging in Galar right now...

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:52.960
...seem to be connected
to the legend of that hero!

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:56.670
So I’m going to the ruins
in Turf Town with Ms. Sonia,

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:58.880
to solve the mystery
of the legend!

00:20:58.880 --> 00:20:59.890
Got it!

00:20:59.890 --> 00:21:04.030
Let’s both do all we can for now,
and meet up later!

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.260
Okay!

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:08.580
Satoshi! It’s in sight!

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:10.500
Right!

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:11.330
See ya later!

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:13.660
Hey, hold... on...

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:14.830
Honestly...

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:18.080
Your friend, he’s with Dande?

00:21:18.490 --> 00:21:20.420
Yeah. That’s what he said.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:26.590
Let’s go, Satoshi!

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:27.430
Right!

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:33.150
Something is beginning to unfold
in the Galar Region.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:36.940
At their destinations,
what will Satoshi and Go find...?

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:40.100
Despair? Or hope?

00:21:50.860 --> 00:21:51.530
Pikachu!

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:52.400
Utsubot!

00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:53.110
Transel!

00:21:53.110 --> 00:21:53.910
Lugia!

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:54.700
Achamo!

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:55.490
Morpeko!

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:56.200
Koduck!

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:57.080
Cleffy!

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:57.780
Eevee!

00:21:57.780 --> 00:21:58.530
Ishitsubute!

00:21:58.530 --> 00:21:59.200
Teppouo!

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:00.120
Onisuzume!

00:22:00.120 --> 00:22:00.830
Metagross!

00:22:00.830 --> 00:22:01.870
Subame!

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:02.540
Me...

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:03.790
Metamon!

00:22:19.760 --> 00:22:20.560
Pikachu!

00:22:20.560 --> 00:22:21.390
Usohachi!

00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:22.100
Chicorita!

00:22:22.100 --> 00:22:22.890
Tamatama!

00:22:22.890 --> 00:22:23.640
Mamepato!

00:22:23.640 --> 00:22:24.480
Togedemaru!

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:25.230
Lucario!

00:22:25.230 --> 00:22:26.020
Odoshishi!

00:22:26.020 --> 00:22:26.810
Seadra!

00:22:26.810 --> 00:22:27.440
Laplace!

00:22:27.440 --> 00:22:28.270
Starmie!

00:22:28.270 --> 00:22:29.070
Miniryu!

00:22:29.070 --> 00:22:29.860
Windie!

00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:30.570
Iwark!

00:22:30.570 --> 00:22:31.400
Kucheat!

00:22:31.400 --> 00:22:32.150
Togekiss!

00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:32.900
Sleep!

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:33.650
Ptera!

00:22:33.650 --> 00:22:34.490
Raikou!

00:22:34.490 --> 00:22:35.240
U’u!

00:22:35.240 --> 00:22:36.030
Wooloo!

00:22:36.030 --> 00:22:36.820
Ruriri!

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:37.570
Leafia!

00:22:37.570 --> 00:22:38.370
Armorgaw!

00:22:38.370 --> 00:22:39.160
Abagoura!

00:22:39.160 --> 00:22:39.950
Latias!

00:22:39.950 --> 00:22:40.700
Spear!

00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:41.450
Agnome!

00:22:41.450 --> 00:22:42.200
Muma!

00:22:42.200 --> 00:22:43.290
Madatsubomi!

00:22:43.710 --> 00:22:44.750
Mew!

00:23:07.190 --> 00:23:09.620
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:11.120
Go!

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:16.320
Wishing Stars, and Galar particles...
That’s the secret of Daimax?!

00:23:16.320 --> 00:23:19.990
And I intend to do everything
within my power,

00:23:19.990 --> 00:23:23.630
in order for this marvelous view
to last a thousand years.

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:26.890
Chairman Rose will stop at nothing
to achieve his goals.

00:23:26.890 --> 00:23:29.440
The Pokémon aren’t rampaging
because they want to, either!

00:23:29.910 --> 00:23:31.160
Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.160 --> 00:23:32.900
Sword and Shield

00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:34.440
The Black Night
